25,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears our hard surfacing fails quickly, while water-based infrastructure from years ago is still holding up. However, recent planting efforts were a disaster due to poor aftercare.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"We have a problem with the soil; firms are warning about clay and slippage. Also, we can't close the main gate or center without total site hoarding.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Mio,,"The habitat fund is generous but very restrictive—it only pays for plants and water. Meanwhile, the cost to maintain green space is tripling compared to paving.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"Our internal staff is depleted, though we have casuals for weekends. Interestingly, we have active volunteers for both habitat work and sports league refereeing.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Minako,,"People are using the park as a thoroughfare to the tram, sticking to firm ground. Also, the drainage is failing and the heat is becoming an issue.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mio, if the habitat fund covers the capital but the upkeep is triple for green space, we are creating a future budget hole.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Minako, if people are sticking to firm ground, any plan that forces them into soft margins might fail or be destroyed.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Mio,,"Exactly, Benjamin! I'm worried we'll be broke in three years. @Asuka, can volunteers offset those high maintenance costs?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"Only for specific tasks, Mio. Habitat and sports are covered, but general groundskeeping is still a struggle with only seven staff left.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Misaki, the clay slippage you mentioned combined with my drainage data suggests that heavy earth-moving or complex water features could be risky.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, the fact that we have sports volunteers is a strong point if we consider active recreation.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Minako, if the center cannot be hoarded, we should look for a plan that focuses on the southern area to keep the park open.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, the earlier programme showed that paving is patched constantly. Maybe ""cheap"" surfacing is actually more expensive over time?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Minako, does the tram-stop traffic make a central plaza more logical than a woodland?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Minako,,"It does, but the heat readings suggest we need shade, not just a paved oven.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
