49,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
50,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The candidates are A: Market Plaza, B: Woodland Walk, C: Wetland Restoration, and D: Sports Terraces. I lean toward C; the earlier works show water infrastructure lasts.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"I cannot support C or B if they require deep digging in clay. D is in the south, which fits the hoarding notes perfectly.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Mio,,A and D are cheaper to maintain per hectare. B and C would be a financial nightmare given the upkeep ledger.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"D is the most sustainable for staffing. We already have volunteers for sports, and it doesn't require the specialist care that B or C would.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Minako,,A is too hot and ignores the drainage issues. C is risky with the clay. D provides a firm surface for the tram commuters and uses the south side.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, if D is the only one that allows the park to stay open during construction, that is a significant logical advantage.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Misaki,,It is. And the earth-moving for courts is generally shallower than for ponds or dense woodland.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Asuka, if the sports volunteers are already there, does that mean the city doesn't have to buy in as many services for D?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Asuka,,Precisely. It leverages existing community assets rather than relying on a depleted city roll.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, while you like the longevity of water works, the current drainage callouts suggest we shouldn't add more complex water systems now.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"That is a fair point, Minako. The immediate operational risk outweighs the long-term structural preference.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I'm voting for D. It's the most deliverable option.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'm voting for D too! It's the safest for the budget.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Asuka,,D is my choice. It fits our staffing reality.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Minako,,I agree. D respects the traffic patterns and the site constraints. I vote D.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I will align with the group. D is the most rational choice given the combined constraints. I vote D.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
